=== 2. WON: does it raise an enquiry or quotation by itself? ===
    [opportunity-move -> WON] success: Won. Raise the order when the customer confirms.
    {"id":1,"ref":"OPP-2026-0001","status":"WON","stage_id":12,"value":100000,"partner_id":666,"contract_id":null,"call_id":null} ; inquiries +0, quotations +0
    [opportunity-move WON -> OPEN stage (reopen?)] error: That opportunity is already won.
    [opportunity-move WON -> LOST] error: That opportunity is already won.
    [opportunity-edit on WON deal (value 1, renamed)] success: Saved.
    after edit: {"id":1,"ref":"OPP-2026-0001","status":"WON","stage_id":12,"value":1,"partner_id":666,"contract_id":null,"call_id":null}
    history rows for the edit (activities): 0 ; all activity subjects: ["Opportunity OPP-2026-0001 opened \u2014 Deal won directly","Moved to Won \u2014 won"]

=== 3. two alternative quotations on one deal: one is LOST, the other is later ACCEPTED ===
    [link quote A] (no flash)
    [link quote B] (no flash)
    [MM marks A LOST (client chose option B)] success: Quotation moved to Lost / regretted.
    deal after A lost: {"id":2,"ref":"OPP-2026-0002","status":"LOST","stage_id":13,"value":100000,"partner_id":666,"contract_id":null,"call_id":null}
    [MM marks B ACCEPTED] success: quote marked accepted. Acme Probe is now linked to the client master, 1 contact(s) carried across. Its line items can now be pulled straight onto a purchase order from the client master. The record is deliberately incomplete — it still needs GSTIN or PAN, an address and a contact mobile number. Comp
    deal after B accepted: {"id":2,"ref":"OPP-2026-0002","status":"LOST","stage_id":13,"value":100000,"partner_id":666,"contract_id":null,"call_id":null}   quote B: #2 Q-00002 r0 cur=1 ACCEPTED total=59000 contract=-

=== 4. deal already LOST by hand, then its quotation is ACCEPTED ===
    [deal -> LOST] success: Recorded as lost, with the reason.
    [quote ACCEPTED] success: quote marked accepted. Acme Probe is now linked to the client master. Its line items can now be pulled straight onto a purchase order from the client master. The record is deliberately incomplete — it still needs GSTIN or PAN, an address and a contact mobile number. Complete it before the first work
    deal: {"id":3,"ref":"OPP-2026-0003","status":"LOST","stage_id":13,"value":100000,"partner_id":666,"contract_id":null,"call_id":null}   quote: #3 Q-00003 r0 cur=1 ACCEPTED total=59000 contract=-

=== 5. one won deal, two contracts: quote-contract AND opportunity-contract ===
    [quote ACCEPTED (wins the deal)] success: quote marked accepted. Acme Probe is now linked to the client master. Its line items can now be pulled straight onto a purchase order from the client master. The record is deliberately incomplete — it still needs GSTIN or PAN, an address and a contact mobile number. Complete it before the first work
